## Scenarios

### Calc session host production isolation

#### keeps the normal terminal owner free of access and capture transports

- Verify: keeps the normal terminal owner free of access and capture transports
- Running the normal terminal owner terminates without a tty
   - Expected: rc equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — no raw-mode terminal diagnostic`
- No listener was bound: the control port is still free afterwards
   - Expected: fd >= 0 is true
- Constructing the session host standalone works without any transport
   - Expected: host.running is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 14 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-OFFICE-001
step("Verify: keeps the normal terminal owner free of access and capture transports")
val control_port = 47611
step("Running the normal terminal owner terminates without a tty")
val rc = run_calc_session_host("/tmp/simple_calc_isolation_absent_sheet.ods")
expect(rc).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — no raw-mode terminal diagnostic
step("No listener was bound: the control port is still free afterwards")
val fd = tcp_listener_bind_fd("127.0.0.1:" + control_port.to_text())
expect(fd >= 0).to_equal(true)
if fd >= 0:
    tcp_fd_close(fd)
step("Constructing the session host standalone works without any transport")
val host = CalcSessionHost.open("/tmp/simple_calc_isolation_absent_sheet.ods")
expect(host.running).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Advanced: confines loopback transport to the explicit access adapter</summary>

#### confines loopback transport to the explicit access adapter

- Verify: confines loopback transport to the explicit access adapter
- The access adapter is the opt-in path that binds the loopback listener
   - Expected: rc equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — same no-terminal diagnostic after binding`
- The loopback listener exists: rebinding the access port now fails
   - Expected: fd < 0 is true
- A different port stays free, proving only the access port was bound
   - Expected: other >= 0 is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 14 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-OFFICE-001
step("Verify: confines loopback transport to the explicit access adapter")
val access_port = 47613
step("The access adapter is the opt-in path that binds the loopback listener")
val rc = run_calc_access_session_host(access_port, "/tmp/simple_calc_isolation_absent_sheet.ods")
expect(rc).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — same no-terminal diagnostic after binding
step("The loopback listener exists: rebinding the access port now fails")
val fd = tcp_listener_bind_fd("127.0.0.1:" + access_port.to_text())
expect(fd < 0).to_equal(true)  # oracle: -1 — the access adapter holds the port
step("A different port stays free, proving only the access port was bound")
val other = tcp_listener_bind_fd("127.0.0.1:47615")
expect(other >= 0).to_equal(true)
if other >= 0:
    tcp_fd_close(other)
```

</details>


